   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "Each LED's anode goes through a 220 ohm resistor (resistor straddles the centre gap) to its Arduino pin 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2 respectively (left to right in the image); cathodes go to the top ground rail via short black wires, and the rail connects to the Uno GND pin beside AREF.",
   "Column numbers are read from the circuit image: LED anode/resistor at columns 7, 10, 13, 16, 19, 22; cathode in the next column. Exact rows and rail hole numbers are approximate; all top ground rail holes are one strip.",
   "The schematic shows the same circuit: pin -> 220 ohm -> LED anode, cathodes common to GND."
  ]
